1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
TRANSITLAB v0.5 | Live public browser capture. Deterministic adapter; real LLM is shadow-only.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
"Add one bus." Each accepted command adds exactly one vehicle to the scene.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:24,000
One candidate -> Schema -> Semantics -> Execution. The inspector exposes the action and state.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Four approaches in an orbitable Three.js world, with an original Blender-authored bus.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:46,000
"Turn the signal red." EW stops; NS receives green after all-red intersection clearance.

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:56,000
"Stop the buses." Manual stopping is explicit state, separate from waiting at a red light.

7
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:04,000
"Let the buses continue." They resume only where the traffic controller grants right-of-way.

8
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:14,000
"Make it rain." Validated weather changes the rendering and a simplified speed policy.

9
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:24,000
"Make it snow heavily." Accepted as snow mode: snowfall, wintry lighting and reduced speed.

10
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:36,000
"Make it foggy." Visibility changes in the same interactive world, not a replacement image.

11
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,000
"Restore clear weather." Every accepted change remains visible in the action trace.

12
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Animation paused for comparison. Now request an unsupported change: "Make meteors fall."

13
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,000
REJECTED at schema. The full before/after state is identical; nothing executes.

14
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Event Log: original command, validation stage, rejection reason, state snapshots and build fingerprint.

15
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Language proposes. Validators decide. The world responds. Real LLM execution remains disabled.
